  "_metadata": {
    "synthetic": true,
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic parameters for synthetic longitudinal drug modeling. PK: 1-compartment models (oral with first-order absorption, IV bolus). PD: Emax sigmoid model E = Emax * C^gamma / (EC50^gamma + C^gamma). All values approximate published population PK/PD estimates — NOT fitted to any specific trial.",
    "citation_note": "Parameters informed by published PopPK/PD models and FDA labels. Donepezil: Tiseo 1998, Rogers 1998; Memantine: Periclou 2006; Lecanemab: van Dyck 2023, Swanson 2021; Levodopa: Contin 2010; Pramipexole: Wright 1997; Fluoxetine: Altamura 1994; Venlafaxine: Troy 1997; Riluzole: Groeneveld 2003; Edaravone: Yoshino 2006; Levetiracetam: Patsalos 2004; Ocrelizumab: Hauser 2017.",
    "pk_model_note": "Oral steady-state trough: Css_trough = (F * Dose * ka) / (Vd * (ka - ke)) * (e^(-ke*tau)/(1-e^(-ke*tau)) - e^(-ka*tau)/(1-e^(-ka*tau))). IV bolus: Css_trough = (Dose/Vd) * e^(-ke*tau) / (1 - e^(-ke*tau)). tau = dosing interval in hours.",
    "iiv_note": "Interindividual variability (IIV) expressed as coefficient of variation (CV). Applied as multiplicative lognormal: theta_i = theta_pop * exp(eta_i), eta_i ~ N(0, omega^2), CV ≈ omega for small omega."
  },
